From c4bcae99f492e382b1935f0d6d116857e9e0021e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <winshyon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:03:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: config-only CLI commands see KBs added with `pyrite kb
 add` (#363)

`search -k`, `kb validate`, `kb schema show|add-type|remove-type|set` and
`schema validate -k` built their config with a bare `load_config()`, which
only knows the KBs in config.yaml, so a KB registered with `pyrite kb add`
answered KB_NOT_FOUND there while `get`, `index sync` and `link` accepted it.

Add `with_registered_kbs()` to `pyrite/cli/context.py`, which merges the
database registry into a loaded config (config.yaml still wins on a name
clash) and closes the index again, and route those commands through it.
`kb validate` and `search --files` without a KB name now enumerate
`config.all_kbs()` so they cover registered KBs as well.

Fixes #363

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
